applier.py:226-235`, `differ.py:44,84`, `fetcher.py:153`, `inbound_collection_diffs.py:60`, `inbound_fields.py:45`, `inbound_translate.py:121`, `invariants.py:68,90`, `last_pass.py:53-64`, `pass_io.py:51,69`, `binding_repository.py:298`, `outbound_pass.py:69`. Loader sites in `src` overall (`git grep -lE 'lazy_load\\(|spec_from_file_location' origin/main -- src`): 47 files — 44 under `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` (every `try: from rebar_reconciler._loader import lazy_load / except ImportError:` prologue plus the hand-rolled loaders above) and 3 outside: `src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py:147-161` (`_ref_lock_module`), `src/rebar/_lib_ops.py:161-173` (`_engine_module`), `src/rebar/mcp_server.py:367-378` (`_load_engine_mode` → `rebar._engine_mode`); plus `src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck_drift.py:31-35` and `bridge_fsck_visibility.py:36-50`. In-process `sys.path.insert(engine_dir)` sites: `_cli/__init__.py:148-151`, `_commands/_repair_pause.py:39-42`, `_commands/doctor_mapping.py:43-45`, `_commands/fsck_repair.py:344-347`. `src/rebar/graph/_loader.py:3` only mentions the idiom historically (no change).\n\n**Scripts (Approach step 6) line cites:** `scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py:143` (`_RECONCILER = Path(\"src/rebar/reconciler\")`), `scripts/check_config_ownership.py:77-85,137`, `scripts/capture_jira_fixtures.py:157-159`, `scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py:39-43`, `scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py:64-82`, `scripts/measure_baseline_normalization.py:67-68,129-130,222`, `scripts/measure_get_rotation_cutover.py:22-24`, `infra/scripts/comment_echo_reclaim_manifest.py:28-30`. Verified as NOT hardcoding the engine dir (untouched): `scripts/check_repo_root_from_package.py`, `scripts/check_repo_root_from_tracker.py`, `scripts/check_tickets_boundary.py`.\n\n**Docs (Approach step 9) line cites:** `docs/user-guide.md:658-661`, `docs/architecture.md:31,72,244-272`, `README.md:289`, `docs/exit-codes.md:55-57`; `docs/code-navigation.md`, `docs/coverage.md`, `docs/config.md`, `docs/reuse-surface.md` (whole-file spelling pass).\n\n**`.github/complexity-baseline.json` (Approach step 10) — the six keys**, re-spelled from `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/...` to `src/rebar/reconciler/...` with ceilings unchanged: `outbound_fields.py::_diff_fields:32`, `applier.py::apply:22`, `binding_walk.py::compute_binding_walk_mutations:27`, `dispatch_one.py::create_one:36`, `inbound_differ.py::_diff_jira_vs_local:16`, `outbound_field_diff.py::diff_canonical_fields:23`. (`.github/mechanism-baseline.json` has 29 `autouse_fixture::tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/...` keys; they are untouched by this story because the test package does not move here — the next story re-spells them.)\n\n**`sys.modules` keys the source registers and tests pre-seed (all deleted by the Approach step 8 codemod):** dotted `rebar_reconciler.{_advisory_lock,mode,request,pass_support,_preflight,alert_store,mutation,config,link_direction,adapters.jira.adf,operation_outcome,failure_policy,git_adapter,observation,create_route,coordinator,ticket_planner,ticket_plan,runtime,retry_budget,reconcile_helpers,rebar_id_audit,persist_phase,pass_io,pass_fuse,manifest_renderer,load_phase,dispatch_one,create_coordinator,create_containment,apply_phase,apply_handlers,applier,_errors,batch_dispatch,binding_store,_ref_lock,_loader,__main__}`; flat keys `reconcile_helpers`, `pass_support`, `reconcile_mutation`, `rebar_reconciler_errors`, `rebar_reconciler__ref_lock_advisory`, `rebar_reconciler_ref_lock_advisory`, `rebar_reconciler_ref_lock_push`, `rebar_reconciler_config`, `rebar_reconciler_alert_store`, `reconcile_selection_binding_store`, `reconcile_run_differs`, `reconcile_config`, `reconcile_classify`, `reconcile_binding_walk`, `_concurrency`, `conflict_resolver`, `config`, `overview`, `rebar._engine_mode`, `rebar_reconciler_classify_fsck`; test-private keys (`applier`, `fetcher`, `reconcile_*`, `rebar_reconciler_advisory_lock`, `rebar_reconciler_mode`, ~60 per-file names). 343 test files / 442 `spec_from_file_location` sites; 149 files `import rebar_reconciler`. `pyproject.toml:691-698` has `testpaths=[\"tests\"]` and no `pythonpath`/`rootdir` — the package rename needs no pytest config change.\n\n**Kept, not deleted (already discharged on origin/main):** `Mode.RECONCILE_CHECK` is absent (`mode.py:39-42`); `_ref_lock.py:717` writer persists `\"dry-run\"` (`_PAUSE_GATED_MODE`, `:591`) and the decoder keeps `_PAUSE_LEGACY_GATED_MODES={\"reconcile-check\"}` (`:592`) — bug `extralegal-durative-beaver` is closed (Gerrit 2728); `mode.py:57` `from_str(\"reconcile-check\")→DRY_RUN` and `_ref_lock.py:592` stay as persisted-pause-blob read compat. `MODE_CAPS` is live (`__main__.py:187`, `apply_planning.py:93`, `load_phase.py:165`, `ticket_planner.py:60`) and the bootstrap modes are live consumers (`reconcile-bridge.yml:59-60`, DC harness `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py:70`, `manifest_renderer.py`) — kept; only the MCP by-path load and the dead `ctx.MODE_CAPS`/`ctx.Mode` handles (`mcp_server.py:599-600`, no registrar reads them) are deleted.\n\n**Release note (BREAKING) for `CHANGELOG.md`:** `python -m rebar_reconciler` becomes `python -m rebar.reconciler`; the top-level `rebar_reconciler` import name is removed with no shim (ADR 0083, ADR 0111); `rebar._engine.engine_env` no longer prepends `PYTHONPATH`.","timestamp":1788807674126973120},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator sanction (recorded on the epic): this change carries a value-preserving key re-spell of the `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/...` keys in `.github/complexity-baseline.json` (S1, 6 keys): prefix rewrite only, ceilings and counts unchanged; state this sanction in the commit message.","timestamp":1788807694029980930},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Cross-epic assignment from the docs/ADR epic (astounding-pictural-cowbird): two comments in modules this story moves cite a design document (`docs/designs/sync-hardening-proposal.md`) that never existed in git history. Rewrite them in this change, at the moved paths (origin/main 083620b0 line numbers):\n\n- `inbound_differ.py:265-266`: replace `# Canonical entries (as of 183fd51ac2; pending consolidation into` / `# _field_contract.py per docs/designs/sync-hardening-proposal.md Item 3):` with `# Canonical entries (as of 183fd51ac2; the per-field symmetry rules live in` / `# _field_contract.py, which names this map; consolidation tracked by story a130-2b7c-429c-43d1):`.\n- `apply_handlers.py:504-505`: replace `evidence feeds the binding-GC design in` / `# docs/designs/sync-hardening-proposal.md Item 4b.` with `evidence feeds binding retirement per ADR 0028 (deletion is proven only by a` / `# direct 404; bug 13eb-c414-0763-4fa1 covers GC of bindings to deleted issues).`\n\nBoth replacement blocks stay accepted by `scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py` (grouped-hex ticket ids present). The docs epic's own story fixes the remaining phantom citations in `scripts/` and `tests/`; after both land, `git grep -n 'sync-hardening-proposal'` over `src scripts tests` is empty.","timestamp":1788807986691990359},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CI-lock fact for the `.github/complexity-baseline.json` re-spell (step 10 of the Approach): the `Complexity-baseline lock` step in `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` runs `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --lock`, which diffs this change's baseline against main's copy at the merge base and rejects ANY added key (`lock_against_base`, `scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:488-511`: \"NEW entry added ... an administrator must override the gate\"). A path re-spell is a removed key plus an added key, so the lock cannot distinguish it from a smuggled new ceiling and will vote `Verified -1` on this change even though `make lint` (`--check`) and `tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py` pass locally. Landing therefore requires the override the lock was designed with (task 47e9): an administrator force-submit of this one change after confirming the lock step is the only red item in its CI run. Agents must not perform that override; the session owner escalates it to the operator. Alternatives considered and rejected: reducing the six functions under the threshold inside a move story (not behaviour-preserving), and teaching the lock about renames (a gate redesign for a one-time move).","timestamp":1788809631417226465},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator decision 2026-09-07 (approved): keep the value-preserving re-spell of the six `.github/complexity-baseline.json` keys in this change. Landing instruction: push for review as its own change; when CI reports `Verified -1` with the `Complexity-baseline lock` step as the ONLY red item, the operator (an administrator) force-submits it, which is the override task 47e9 designed the lock with. The implementing agent must not perform the override; it reports the CI run and hands off. The commit message names the six keys, states that ceilings are unchanged, and cites this decision.","timestamp":1788809962492156489},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Experiment result (2026-09-07, scratch worktree at origin/main 4c77d6f3e96f, `git mv src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler src/rebar/reconciler` only, no import edits):\n- C901 scores are path-independent: after the move `--check` reports the six functions as `new` at the new path with scores 32, 20, 27, 27, 16, 23, identical to their scores at the old path on the clean tree; the old keys bucket `stale`. (`apply` at 20 and `create_one` at 27 are already under their ceilings 22 and 36 on main, so they were already stale there.)\n- The re-spell must RE-SORT the ceilings map, not just substitute the prefix: a plain in-place `sed` fails `--check` with `error: 'ceilings' keys must be sorted`, because `src/rebar/reconciler/...` sorts after `src/rebar/_engine_support/...`, `_ids.py`, `_mcp_reads.py` and the other underscore-prefixed keys. Rewrite the file through `render_baseline` (or `json.dumps(..., indent=2, sort_keys=True)` matching its format); `git diff --stat` then shows 6 insertions, 6 deletions.\n- After the sorted re-spell: `--check` gives `active=33 new=0 increased=0 stale=16`, byte-for-byte the clean tree's summary (the 16 stale rows pre-exist on main and are not this story's to drain), and `pytest tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py -q` passes (87 passed).\n- The lock against main's copy (`--lock --base <main's baseline>`) prints exactly six `complexity-baseline lock: NEW entry added: 'src/rebar/reconciler/...'` lines plus the administrator hint and exits 1; removed old-path entries are not flagged. This confirms the landing instruction above: the lock step is the one expected red item for the operator's force-submit.\n- `rebar._proc.reap_process_group(proc, *, grace, drain, label, logger)` exists at `src/rebar/_proc.py:38`; two thin `_reap_process_group` wrappers in `adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py:507` and `jira_family/wiki_render.py:417` import it lazily and move with the package.","timestamp":1788813374091445754},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Coordination note (2026-09-07): open bug unaware-subwealthy-pintail (f778-6dd7-8913-4043, priority 3, reconciler creates a duplicate ticket and Jira issue when a bound pair loses both its binding and its `rebar-id` label) will be fixed inside `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` modules this story moves. Landing order: either that fix lands before this move (then this story carries it across), or it lands after and is authored against `src/rebar/reconciler/`. A fix in flight during the move must be rebased by its author; `git mv` history keeps `git log --follow` working for the moved files.","timestamp":1788813867955287894},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review round 1 (2026-09-07, BLOCK) findings folded into the revised description: `_commands/bridge_repair.py:158-160` (`_engine_module(\"rebar_reconciler.binding_store\")`) was in Scope with no described rewrite (step 5 now names it); prose references at `timeutils.py:9,11`, `_proc.py:7`, `_operation_config.py:232` and `_bridge_commands.py:32` plus the bare argv string at `_bridge_commands.py:51` were outside the codemod patterns (step 1 now covers bare tokens and quoted names, and those files are in Scope); two `__main__.py` cites were wrong (`install_stderr_handler` is at `:491`, the reconcile-absent no-op branch at `:344-348`; the `_advisory is None` fallback at `:364-371` and the `_load_sibling_keyed`/`_try_load_step` helpers at `:116-160` with call sites `:315,344,358,367,417,493,494,529` are now named); the docs grep is now an explicit edge check. The reviewer also flagged the unit as large for one session (advisory); the operator's force-submit landing instruction stands, so the change stays whole.","timestamp":1788814684537194345},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review round 2 (2026-09-07, BLOCK) folded into the revised description: `src/rebar/_config_sections.py:153,208` (two prose references) and the path literal at `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-asserted-capability.eval.yaml:81` are in step 1's rewrite set and in Scope, with `_config_sections.py`'s non-prose lines assigned to the config epic; the basis sentence now names 4c77d6f3e96f for the `__main__.py` cites.","timestamp":1788816950554208887},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Coordination update: colliding bug fix unaware-subwealthy-pintail has landed and closed. Gerrit change 2834 merged as 02e0fae923d45329a3e1dc1921d70e19484401b8 (Use Jira property for dedup). The package-move epic can now rebase/carry the reconciler changes from the current module paths.","timestamp":1788888306036654001}],"created_at":1788807372317960637,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` is package data imported by path: `_loader.py::lazy_load`, 44 in-package loader prologues, hand-rolled loaders in twelve engine modules (first comment), and the out-of-package loaders `_lib_ops._engine_module` (`:161-173`), `_bridge_commands._ref_lock_module` (`:147-161`), `mcp_server._load_engine_mode` (`:367-378`, the `rebar._engine_mode` fork), `_engine.engine_env`'s PYTHONPATH prepend (`:75-102`) and four `sys.path.insert` sites (step 5). The generic top-level name violates namespace hygiene (`docs/architecture.md:244-272`), the by-path idiom forces a `sys.modules` key contract onto 343 test files, and mypy widens every engine annotation to `Any` (`pyproject.toml:627-634`). Operator decision (2026-09-06), BREAKING: the package becomes `rebar.reconciler` with no re-export shim (ADR 0083, ADR 0111); `python -m rebar.reconciler` replaces the old module name; `engine_env` stops prepending `PYTHONPATH`. Cites are on origin/main 4c77d6f3e96f; the first comment's in-package cites are from 083620b0 and shift by up to 41 lines.\n\n## Approach\n1. `git mv src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler src/rebar/reconciler`. A throwaway codemod rewrites, in `src`, `scripts`, `infra`, `tests`: `from rebar_reconciler`, `import rebar_reconciler`, quoted `\"rebar_reconciler\"` and `\"rebar_reconciler.<x>\"` strings (including the argv element at `_cli/_bridge_commands.py:51`), and the bare tokens `rebar_reconciler` and `rebar._engine.rebar_reconciler` in docstrings and comments (`src/rebar/timeutils.py:9,11`, `src/rebar/_proc.py:7`, `src/rebar/_operation_config.py:232`, `src/rebar/_config_sections.py:153,208`, `_bridge_commands.py:32`, the path literal `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-asserted-capability.eval.yaml:81`, and the in-package prose), to `rebar.reconciler`.\n2. Delete `_loader.py`; replace every `try/except ImportError` loader prologue and every `lazy_load(...)`/`_load_*` call with a plain `from rebar.reconciler import x` at module scope (function-local where a cycle exists), keeping the same names so `monkeypatch.setattr` targets survive. In `__main__.py` delete `_load_sibling_keyed` (`:116-139`) and `_try_load_step` (`:141-160`) with their call sites at `:315,344,358,367,417,493,494,529`, the reconcile-absent no-op branch at `:344-348` and the `_advisory is None` fallback at `:364-371`.\n3. Delete the `__main__.py:49-56` bootstrap fallback; `install_stderr_handler(\"rebar_reconciler\")` at `:491` becomes `\"rebar\"`; delete the `__init__.py` NullHandler (the `rebar` root has one).\n4. `src/rebar/_engine.py::engine_env` (`:75-102`): drop the PYTHONPATH prepend; it only pins `REBAR_ROOT`. `engine_dir()` stays for `jira-capability-probe.py` and `resources/`; its docstring and error text stop naming the reconciler.\n5. Delete `_lib_ops._engine_module` and rewrite its consumers: `_lib_ops.py` imports `rebar.reconciler.{projects_store,pass_support,__main__,mode,last_pass,_ref_lock,access_check}` directly; `_commands/bridge_repair.py:158-160` becomes `from rebar.reconciler import binding_store`; `_bridge_commands.py:147-161` (`_ref_lock_module`) and `:188-189` become `from rebar.reconciler import _ref_lock, last_pass`; `mcp_server.py:359-378,599-600` deleted (no registrar reads `ctx.MODE_CAPS`/`ctx.Mode`; `scripts/check_mcp_library_parity.py:130-131` and `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py:97-98` drop the kwargs); `_bridge_runner.py:146-151` becomes `from rebar.reconciler.__main__ import _Disposition`; the `sys.path.insert` sites `_cli/__init__.py:144-151`, `_commands/{_repair_pause.py:37-42,doctor_mapping.py:41-45,fsck_repair.py:342-347}` and the loaders in `_engine_support/bridge_fsck_{drift.py:31-35,visibility.py:28-50}` become plain imports; `src/rebar/_engine/jira-capability-probe.py:25-26` imports `rebar.reconciler.*`.\n6. Eight scripts that hardcode the directory are re-pointed to `src/rebar/reconciler` (list in the first comment).\n7. `pyproject.toml:567` per-file T201 ignore becomes `\"src/rebar/reconciler/*\"`; comments at `:14,68,509,613,627-634` updated.\n8. Tests (mechanical only): every `spec_from_file_location(<key>, <engine path>)` helper becomes `importlib.import_module(\"rebar.reconciler.<mod>\")`; every `sys.modules[...]` seed, `_ENGINE_DIR` and `sys.path.insert` is deleted; `patch(\"rebar_reconciler.x.y\")` strings become `\"rebar.reconciler.x.y\"`; tests that needed a fresh module copy use `monkeypatch.setattr` on the shared module (no `importlib.reload` of `rebar.reconciler.*`). `tests/_engine_path.py` keeps only `repo_root()` (the next story deletes its engine functions); `tests/unit/test_engine_dir.py:27`'s old-path assertion is removed.\n9. Docs: the eight maintained docs and `README.md` listed in the first comment spell `python -m rebar.reconciler` and `rebar.reconciler`; `CHANGELOG.md` BREAKING entry; regenerate `docs/env-vars.md` with `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py`.\n10. `.github/complexity-baseline.json`: re-spell the 6 engine keys to `src/rebar/reconciler/...` with ceilings unchanged and the map RE-SORTED (`reconciler/` sorts after the underscore keys; unsorted fails `--check`); an operator-sanctioned maintenance edit recorded on the epic and in the commit message. The CI lock step rejects the six added keys by design; the operator force-submits this change (landing instruction in the comments).\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/reconciler/**` (moved), `src/rebar/_engine.py`, `src/rebar/_engine/jira-capability-probe.py`, `src/rebar/_lib_ops.py`, `src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py`, `src/rebar/mcp_server.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py` (lines 144-151 only), `src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/{_repair_pause,doctor_mapping,fsck_repair,bridge_repair}.py`, `src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck_{drift,visibility}.py`, prose-only edits in `src/rebar/{timeutils.py,_proc.py,_operation_config.py,_logging.py,_config_schema.py,_config_sections.py}` and `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-asserted-capability.eval.yaml`, `.github/complexity-baseline.json`, the scripts, docs, and tests listed above. Out of scope: `_config_sources.py`, `config.py`, `_deprecations.py` and every non-prose line of `_config_sections.py` (config epic); the rest of `_cli/` (CLI epic); the test-side loader complex and test-package rename (next story); any engine behaviour change.\n\n## Testing\nHappy: `python -c \"import rebar.reconciler, rebar.reconciler.__main__\"`; `python -m rebar.reconciler --help` exits 0 with no PYTHONPATH; `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler tests/interfaces tests/scripts -q`; `make import-walk`; `make typecheck` (fix newly resolvable annotation errors at site). Edge: `git grep -nE 'rebar_reconciler|lazy_load\\(|_engine/rebar_reconciler' -- src scripts infra tests` returns only frozen fixture corpora under `tests/fixtures/`, and the same grep over `docs README.md ':!docs/adr' ':!docs/experiments' ':!docs/archive'` returns nothing; `python -c \"import rebar, rebar_reconciler\"` fails (`tests/unit/test_engine_dir.py::test_library_path_exposes_no_generic_top_level_engine_names` passes); `test_transport_param_typing_cc77.py` updated for the now-checkable port annotations; `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` prints `new=0 increased=0`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` and `_loader.py` do not exist and `src/rebar/reconciler/__init__.py` exists, verified by `git ls-tree`.\n- [ ] `git grep -nE 'spec_from_file_location|lazy_load\\(' -- src` returns only the `src/rebar/graph/_loader.py` docstring, and the two edge greps above are empty.\n- [ ] `python -m rebar.reconciler preview --repo-root <tmp>` runs from a fresh venv with no `PYTHONPATH` (`tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py` subprocess case).\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0; `.github/complexity-baseline.json` has 6 sorted `src/rebar/reconciler/` keys with unchanged ceilings (`check_complexity_baseline.py --check` prints `new=0 increased=0`).\n- [ ] `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check` is clean.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/","reason":"package moved from _engine, loaders deleted"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/","reason":"removed"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine.py","reason":"engine_env drops PYTHONPATH"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/jira-capability-probe.py","reason":"import path"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_ops.py","reason":"delete _engine_module"},{"path":"src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py","reason":"import _Disposition directly"},{"path":"src/rebar/mcp_server.py","reason":"delete _load_engine_mode + ctx.MODE_CAPS/Mode"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","reason":"lines 144-151 plain import"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py","reason":"delete _ref_lock_module; -m rebar.reconciler"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/_repair_pause.py","reason":"plain import"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/doctor_mapping.py","reason":"plain import"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck_repair.py","reason":"plain import"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/bridge_repair.py","reason":"plain import"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck_drift.py","reason":"plain import"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck_visibility.py","reason":"plain import"},{"path":"src/rebar/_logging.py","reason":"docstring"},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_schema.py","reason":"comment :665 only"},{"path":"pyproject.toml","reason":"T201 glob + comments"},{"path":"scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"scripts/check_config_ownership.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"scripts/capture_jira_fixtures.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"scripts/measure_baseline_normalization.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"scripts/measure_get_rotation_cutover.py","reason":"path"},{"path":"scripts/check_mcp_library_parity.py","reason":"drop kwargs"},{"path":"scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py","reason":"drop kwargs"},{"path":"infra/scripts/comment_echo_reclaim_manifest.py","reason":"path"},{"path":".github/complexity-baseline.json","reason":"6 keys re-spelled, ceilings unchanged (operator-sanctioned)"},{"path":"tests/","reason":"mechanical import codemod (343 files)"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"-m rebar.reconciler"},{"path":"docs/architecture.md","reason":"package name"},{"path":"docs/exit-codes.md","reason":"path"},{"path":"docs/code-navigation.md","reason":"path"},{"path":"docs/coverage.md","reason":"path"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"path"},{"path":"docs/reuse-surface.md","reason":"path"},{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"regenerated"},{"path":"README.md","reason":":289"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"BREAKING entry"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","ebf5-5d21-0124-4313"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"ebf5-5d21-0124-4313","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_id":"bf96-5776-6a97-420f","ticket_type":"story","title":"Move the reconciler to rebar.reconciler and delete every by-path loader","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d7739122-264d-4057-b6ba-ec7c55d9e232","2dc6ad0b-c536-4efb-9d59-09715a6b7e87","e204a0c0-a69f-47b8-aed7-6925d5d62547","6accbb1a-d8c7-4fc0-ac61-d44190e8d82d","cb39457b-cb6e-48f8-8697-5de593b8a3dd","fd4a737f-6293-44cc-879f-40e5c02392d0","7844e48c-cbee-4f8a-89ab-afa8930f0de1","8016a65e-8c64-4221-89af-e373a12fdb66","746857e2-7e89-4236-bb51-f136840a7557","26a39154-bacf-40d8-98e0-831045e4cf95","69ee5cd4-101f-4af7-84f2-b39e7d9b07ed"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788890912991677001,"uuid":"e9a36ab2-9248-46e2-a2d7-bd8e66242cf3"}